  "7709034356": "An accomplished Career Coach and MBA specialist with 16 years of end-to-end experience in guiding students and professionals through complex career transitions, higher education choices, and MBA admissions across India. Currently working with upGrad as a Career Coach, this professional blends deep industry knowledge with structured mentoring to help learners choose the right programs, upskilling paths, and B-schools aligned to their long-term goals.​\n\nKnown for a practical, market-driven approach, the coach has advised a wide spectrum of candidates—from fresh graduates to mid-career professionals—on entrance exams, profile building, program selection, and post-MBA career planning. With strong communication skills and a coaching style that is empathetic yet straightforward, they specialise in breaking down complex choices into clear, actionable roadmaps that maximise career growth and return on investment.​\n\nAt upGrad, the focus is on personalised one-on-one guidance, goal clarity, and ongoing support, ensuring every learner feels supported from the first counselling conversation to final admission or career transition. This combination of rich on-ground counselling experience and exposure to modern, tech-enabled education platforms makes this Career Coach a trusted partner for anyone serious about accelerating their career through the right MBA or upskilling journey.",
  "7709296755": "I’m Varad, an Engineering Admission and Career Counsellor dedicated to helping students navigate this important phase with clarity and confidence.\nI guide students in selecting the right college and branch across Maharashtra, keeping their rank, interests, and goals in mind.\nI provide step-by-step support during CAP rounds, including detailed cutoff analysis and accurate option filling.\nMy counselling style is simple, honest, and student-friendly, so students feel comfortable asking questions.\nI focus on reducing stress by explaining every option clearly and practically.\nMy aim is to help students make well-informed decisions they feel confident about in the long run.",
  "7756062343": "As an engineering counsellor operating in Maharashtra, you play a pivotal role in guiding aspiring engineers through their educational and career paths. Your expertise lies in understanding the diverse engineering disciplines and the various institutions available in the state. You provide personalized advice to students, helping them identify their strengths, interests, and career goals.\n\nYour responsibilities include conducting one-on-one counselling sessions, organizing workshops, and providing information on entrance exams, admission processes, and scholarship opportunities. You stay updated on industry trends and job market demands, ensuring that your guidance is relevant and beneficial.\n\nAdditionally, you foster relationships with educational institutions and industry professionals, creating a network that can support your clients in their academic and professional journeys. Your commitment to empowering students and helping them make informed decisions is at the heart of your counselling practice.",
  "7768038702": "A compassionate and approachable Career Counsellor. Provide education counselling and best guidance. Helps learners explore their passions, strengths, and opportunities through interactive sessions designed to simplify decision-making and boost confidence.",
  "7770004914": "Pallavi Rajadhyax is a quintessential education counsellor. She graduated in Commerce and followed it up with a double MBA with specializations in Marketing and Finance, both from Pune University. \n\nPallavi started as a Finance professional working with marquee names like Citibank and ICICI Prudential. However she found her calling in teaching and has spent 2 decades as an educator teaching in MBA Colleges as well as High Schools. She has also taught as a tutor to students of French across multiple boards and also instructed working professionals.\n\nPallavi has also worked as a Career Counsellor and guided many students to admissions and scholarships across multiple foreign universities both at an Undergraduate and Post-Graduate Level.\n\nShe has professional certifications in French including DELF (French Ministry of National Education) and has completed a Certificate Course in French in Belgium and Alliance Francaise, Pune.  Pallavi also has a Global Career Counselling Certification offered by the University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA extension) and a Green Belt global Career Certification offered \n\nPallavi rounds off her formidable expertise as a counsellor with a deep knowledge of the culture of Western Countries through her stay in Europe and USA. This combined with her patience and ability in partnering with students and parents alike make her a very effective Counsellor.",
  "7841055591": "I’m Akash, an Engineering Admission and Career Counsellor dedicated to helping students navigate this important phase with clarity and confidence.\nI guide students in selecting the right college and branch across Maharashtra, keeping their rank, interests, and goals in mind.\nI provide step-by-step support during CAP rounds, including detailed cutoff analysis and accurate option filling.\nMy counselling style is simple, honest, and student-friendly, so students feel comfortable asking questions.\nI focus on reducing stress by explaining every option clearly and practically.\nMy aim is to help students make well-informed decisions they feel confident about in the long run.",
  "7970721277": "Over the last 2+ years, I’ve worked as a career counsellor, guiding 105+ candidates across MBA, Engineering, and Literature paths.\nAlongside, I run a YouTube channel sharing practical insights on careers, MBA life, and decision-making.\nI am an alumnus of IIM Kozhikode, where I strengthened my understanding of business and product thinking.\nI am working as a Product Manager, in leading NBFC building products at the intersection of users, technology, and business. \nBefore my MBA, I spent 1.5 years at BEL as an EVM Engineer, working on large-scale public systems.\nI hold an Electronics & Communication Engineering degree from PTU.\nCollege also shaped my voice—I worked as a Radio Jockey, learning the art of communication early on.\nCatch me on https://www.linkedin.com/in/shubhangiaryan\nAnd YT channel: https://youtube.com/@shubhangi_says",
  "8080471633": "I’m shravan, an engineering admission and career counsellor focused on helping students navigate their options with clarity.\nI provide guidance for college and branch selection across Maharashtra, considering ranks, cutoffs, and career goals.\nMy support includes CAP round strategies, cutoff analysis, and precise option filling.\nI emphasize honest advice, practical insights, and a stress-free approach to admissions.\nMy goal is to help students make confident decisions for a strong academic future.",
